# Facing-normal + normal-atlas A/B, at NOON.
#
# PREREQUISITE: a THROWAWAY clone of an explored save, --var WORLD=<name>. See
# lightmode-world.vv for the clone command and why it must be a save you can lose.
#
# WHY NOON, and why every earlier attempt measured nothing:
# the surface normal is consumed in exactly two places in sprite.frag --
#   * the emitter loops   (lambert, gated by nrm_amount)
#   * the sun term        (sun_lambert, line ~767)
# and the sun term is multiplied by `sun_intensity`. In the shipped save that value was
# MEASURED at ~0.002 by dumping it as flat grey (0.36/255 against a forced-white 192.6
# reference), with n_emit=2. So the frame had no directional light whatsoever: its
# daylight-looking luma of 57.7 comes from the NON-directional sky term. Forcing a +-3.0
# normal tilt on every sprite in that scene moved 0.28% of pixels, and killing the sun's
# N.L outright moved 0.13% -- both indistinguishable from the 0.02% same-state null.
# Those were measurements of the scene, not of the feature.
#
# A normal only becomes visible when something DIRECTIONAL illuminates it, so this
# scenario puts the sun overhead first and measures afterwards.
#
# Hour is set through the debug menu with the sequence proven in light-scene.vv:
#   ESC -> c (Debug Menu) -> m -> t -> h, clear the field, type 12, ENTER, ESC out.
launch --dont-debugmsg --world ${WORLD}
waitlog "opened document .*sidebar_hud.rml" timeout=300000
focus
settle timeout=25000

# The window resizes shortly after the world loads (measured 1920x1080, then 2560x1440
# ~1.5 s later), so discard a warm-up capture and settle again: a size change between two
# measured shots aborts the run.
shot warmup avg=4
wait 6000
settle timeout=15000

# Conservative rect well inside the map viewport. The HUD sidebar and message bar are
# drawn on is_lit=false segments and are not part of the lighting composite at all, so
# including them would dilute every number with pixels the feature cannot touch.
rect play 0.25,0.12,0.55,0.80

# ---- set the clock to 12:00 ----
key "{ESC}"
wait 1800
key "c"
wait 2000
key "m"
wait 1800
key "t"
wait 2000
key "h"
wait 1500
key "{BACKSPACE}"
wait 300
key "{BACKSPACE}"
wait 300
key "1"
wait 400
key "2"
wait 500
key "{ENTER}"
wait 1500
key "{ESC}"
wait 1200
key "{ESC}"
wait 1200
key "{ESC}"
wait 4000

settle timeout=15000
shot noon avg=12
stats noon in=play

# Paired same-state capture: without a null there is no way to tell a real difference
# between two BUILDS from frame-to-frame shimmer (this scene has animated foliage sway
# and flicker, which move pixels on their own).
shot noon_again avg=12
diff noon noon_again as=same_state in=play

# The clock change MUST have landed, or `noon` is just a second copy of the unlit frame
# and the whole A/B silently compares nothing. A sunless frame measured luma 57.7; noon
# has to be materially brighter than that.
assert noon.luma > 70

log
stop
